  "chapter": {
    "number": 62,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(63) A Psalm of David, when he was in the wilderness of Idumea."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O God, my God, I cry to you early; my soul has thirsted for you: how often has my flesh longed after you, in a barren and trackless and dry land!",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Thus have I appeared before you in the sanctuary, that I might see your power and your glory.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For your mercy is better than",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 112
          },
          {
            "text": "life: my lips shall praise you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Thus will I bless you during my life: I will lift up my hands in your name.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let my soul be filled as with marrow and fatness; and my joyful lips shall praise your name.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 113
          },
          {
            "text": "Forasmuch as I have remembered you on my bed: in the early seasons I have meditated on you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you have been my helper, and in the shelter of your wings will I rejoice.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My soul has",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 114
          },
          {
            "text": "kept very close behind you: your right hand has upheld me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But they vainly sought after my soul; they shall go into the lowest parts o the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall be delivered up to the power of the sword; they shall be portions for foxes.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But the king shall rejoice in God; every one that swears by him shall be praised; for the mouth of them that speak unjust things has been stopped.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 112,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. lives.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 62,
          "verse": 3
        }
